\f1\fs22 Hayley stiffened in the armchair she\'92d fallen asleep in, blinked and got to her feet. Her head quickly stopped spinning. A warning dialogue was flashing on the centre screen at the station she had no recollection of abandoning. A seismic disturbance had been detected. Hayley hit the space bar; a panoramic screen on the opposite wall lit up, showing a view of a wrecked Traverse pod that looked like it had been flipped and dumped. The maglev rail had been wrenched up and a sizeable section was pointing at the ceiling.\
Hayley cleared the cheese platter and the glasses away and took a seat at the workstation. She started cycling through the camera angles of the wider concourse. Jones clones were binding the hands and feet of Shakti guards and tending to the injured. One clone jumped off the concourse and disappeared down the tunnel. From one angle, Hayley found Chanta chatting to what could have been the High Elvis, but how would Hayley know, really?\
Clearly, the Elvi were coming to be with Sarah, and Tony had ignored Sarah\'92s advice to sit tight.
